    "narrative": "For the Zurich Zebras on May 15, **Yordan Alvarez** (75.69) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.53) anchor our production. **Yordan Alvarez** remains the priority play, as his elite .421 xwOBA overcomes a marginal matchup against Leiter. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a high-upside play driven by a significant 14% boost from dynamic platoon metrics and a 4% efficiency lift due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a prime opportunity to capitalize on our organizational mandate to maximize stolen base potential. **Junior Caminero** (67.27) also grades out strongly, leveraging a favorable matchup against Junk to secure his place as a core contributor today.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins involved **Chase Meidroth** (44.54), who was ultimately pushed to the bench. While his profile was competitive, his projected efficiency fell just short of **Dillon Dingler** and **Carson Benge** when factoring in the situational lineup placement of our starters. We are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Trea Turner** (53.83) and **Kyle Schwarber** (52.46); both face the difficult Ashcraft, whose 3.52 xERA is suppressing their base scores significantly. With **Lars Nootbaar** and **Christian Yelich** unavailable, our bench depth is currently limited, necessitating a careful approach to our game caps as we navigate this stretch of matchups.",
